    "specPath": "specs/039-model-backed-rank/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 002 and 005 (R-16), for #76 child C2. Adds a `rank` step kind with three declared modes (listwise, pointwise, pairwise) over a bounded candidate pool, a distinct `ModelRanking` value kind that records partial rankings, dropped ids with reasons, scores scoped to one ranking request and pairwise win counts, optional identity-bearing position-bias controls driven by a named seeded generator, and a `select` step that fills k positions from a model ranking and, when it is short or its backend failed, from a declared exact ordering, with per-position origin and derivation. Pairwise schedules are deterministic and bounded by `max_comparisons`; cycles are resolved by win count, then an exact tie-break, and counted. The constructs join the #76 track versions (`rustev.definition/2`, `rustev.plan/3`, `rustev.evidence/2`); the backend descriptor gains an optional `ranking` member. The rules backend (spec 005) answers pointwise `rank` for the swap test. Bedrock (spec 030) admits its reserved `rank` value under 030 3.12. Jev (specs 012 and 022) keeps R-28: rankings over Jev answers stay composed in plans and feed `select` unchanged. Plans that use none of this keep byte-identical identities. Approved (A-36); implementation is in progress.\n",
    "title": "Model-backed rank and deterministic backfill (amends 002 and 005)"
  },
